<% content_for :title, "Rate Limits" %>

<div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Rate Limits</h1>
  <p class="text-xl text-slate-400 mb-8">
    Understanding and working with API rate limits.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Current Limits</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">
    All API requests require authentication. We use a sliding window with burst support, allowing
    short bursts of requests while enforcing overall limits:
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose mb-8">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/30">
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Window</th>
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Limit</th>
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">10 seconds</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">60 requests</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Allows quick bursts</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">1 minute</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">200 requests</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Smooths request patterns</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">1 hour</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">1,000 requests</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Overall cap</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Per request</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">100 items</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">Bulk endpoint limit</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-pd-secondary border border-slate-700/20 rounded-xl p-4 not-prose mb-8">
    <div class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">How it works</div>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
      All limits apply simultaneously. You can burst up to 60 requests in 10 seconds, but you can't
      exceed 200 in a minute or 1,000 in an hour. This lets you make quick bulk checks while preventing abuse.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Upstream Service Limits</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">
    phish.directory aggregates threat intelligence from multiple sources. Each source has its own rate limits:
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose mb-8">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/30">
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Service</th>
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Per Minute</th>
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Per Hour</th>
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Per Day</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">VirusTotal</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">4</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">-</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">500</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">URLScan</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">60</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">100</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">1,000</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Google Safe Browsing</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">100</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">-</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">10,000</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-100">Walshy</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">30</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">500</td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-400">-</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-pd-secondary border border-slate-700/20 rounded-xl p-4 not-prose mb-8">
    <div class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">Graceful Degradation</div>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
      When an upstream service is rate-limited, we still return results from available services.
      The response includes a <code class="text-cyan-accent">rate_limited_services</code> field
      indicating which sources were temporarily unavailable.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Rate Limit Headers</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">
    When rate limited, responses include these headers:
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose mb-8">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/30">
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Header</th>
          <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 text-slate-400 font-semibold">Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">X-RateLimit-Limit</code></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">Maximum requests allowed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">X-RateLimit-Remaining</code></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">Requests remaining (0 when limited)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">X-RateLimit-Reset</code></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">Unix timestamp when the limit resets</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-700/20">
          <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-accent">Retry-After</code></td>
          <td class="py-3 px-4 text-slate-300">Seconds to wait before retrying</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Rate Limit Response</h2>
  <p class="text-slate-300 mb-4">
    When you exceed the rate limit, you'll receive a <code class="bg-pd-tertiary px-2 py-1 rounded text-sm">429 Too Many Requests</code> response:
  </p>

  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
<pre class="text-slate-100">{
  "error": "Rate limit exceeded. Retry later."
}</pre>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Best Practices</h2>

  <ul class="text-slate-300 space-y-3 mb-8">
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="text-cyan-accent mt-1">✓</span>
      <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Use bulk endpoints</strong> — Check up to 100 domains/URLs in a single request instead of making individual calls</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="text-cyan-accent mt-1">✓</span>
      <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Monitor rate limit headers</strong> — Track your usage and slow down before hitting limits</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="text-cyan-accent mt-1">✓</span>
      <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Implement exponential backoff</strong> — When rate limited, wait progressively longer between retries</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="text-cyan-accent mt-1">✓</span>
      <span><strong class="text-slate-100">Cache results</strong> — Store results locally to avoid redundant API calls</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100 mt-8 mb-4">Example: Handling Rate Limits</h2>

  <div class="bg-pd-tertiary rounded-xl p-5 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
<pre class="text-slate-100">async function checkWithRetry(domain, maxRetries = 3) {
  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < maxRetries; attempt++) {
    const response = await fetch(
      'https://phish.directory/api/v1/domain/check',
      {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Authorization': 'Bearer pdat_your_api_key',
          'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({ domain })
      }
    );

    if (response.status === 429) {
      const retryAfter = response.headers.get('Retry-After') || 60;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, retryAfter * 1000));
      continue;
    }

    return response.json();
  }

  throw new Error('Max retries exceeded');
}</pre>
  </div>
</div>
